   $q$The prefix e- means "out," and the Latin root rupt means "break." What is an "eruption" of a volcano?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A slow cooling of lava into solid rock","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"A long period when the volcano stays quiet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"A bursting out of magma from inside the volcano","is_correct":true},{"text":"A measurement of how much the ground shakes","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-related-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A bursting out of magma from inside the volcano$q$, $q$E plus rupt means "break out," so an eruption is when magma bursts out of the volcano. A measurement of shaking is what a seismograph makes, not what an eruption is.$q$, 'draft', 'bb8241f0-37f6-5ff9-8156-bf2bbffe9f5a')
