   $q$The Greek root tele means "far," and graph means "write." What was the "telegraph"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A device for seeing objects that are very far away","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"A long fence of wires that marked the edge of a city","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A device for sending written messages over long distances","is_correct":true},{"text":"A machine for printing many copies of a newspaper","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-first-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A device for sending written messages over long distances$q$, $q$Tele plus graph means "far writing," and the passage describes messages sent through wires and written down at the other end. A device for seeing far away is a telescope, which shares tele but not graph.$q$, 'draft', '8b40a0a8-dbf0-598f-8321-e207b978a0c5')
