   $q$The prefix trans- means "across," and the Latin root mit means "send." What did newspapers do when they used telegraph lines to "transmit stories"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They shortened the stories to save paper","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They sent the stories from one place to another","is_correct":true},{"text":"They corrected spelling mistakes in the stories","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"They hid the stories so no one could read them","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They sent the stories from one place to another$q$, $q$Trans plus mit means "send across," and the telegraph's job was to carry messages between cities. Shortening the stories might save money, but the word itself is about sending, not shortening.$q$, 'draft', '8b40a0a8-dbf0-598f-8321-e207b978a0c5')
