   $q$The Greek root auto means "self." What does it mean that the robots are "automatic"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They move faster than any person could ever walk","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"They are steered by a worker holding a remote control","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"They are powered by the same engines used in cars","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"They work by themselves without a person guiding each move","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They work by themselves without a person guiding each move$q$, $q$Auto means "self," and the passage says each robot "moves on its own to the right shelf." Being steered by a worker is the opposite of acting by itself.$q$, 'draft', '6ba9277d-d8c4-5cce-84b0-02f02a456dc1')
