  ('72523ce6-8936-5094-b320-43821c39968b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The prefix trans- means "across," and the Latin root port means "carry." What do the robots do when they "transport the shelves"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They repair the shelves when they are damaged","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"They carry the shelves from one place to another","is_correct":true},{"text":"They sort the shelves into groups by size","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"They keep the shelves locked in one place","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They carry the shelves from one place to another$q$, $q$Trans plus port means "carry across," and the robots lift each shelf and carry it to a packing station. Repairing is done by workers and technicians, not by the robots moving shelves.$q$, 'draft', '6ba9277d-d8c4-5cce-84b0-02f02a456dc1')
