   $q$The prefix re- means "back," and ject means "throw." What does the system do when it will "reject" a crushed box?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It repairs the box right away at the station","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It prints a new label for the box","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"It refuses the box and sends it away from the main line","is_correct":true},{"text":"It approves the box and sends it on to the buyer","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It refuses the box and sends it away from the main line$q$, $q$To reject is to "throw back," and the passage says the item is pushed onto a separate belt. A worker may later repair it, but the system itself only turns it away.$q$, 'draft', '6ba9277d-d8c4-5cce-84b0-02f02a456dc1')
