  ('0947b7a1-61fa-5c1f-832e-27ced8373093', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In "malfunction," the prefix mal- means "bad" or "badly." Which word uses mal- with the same meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"malt","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"spelling-not-meaning"},{"text":"malnourished","is_correct":true},{"text":"mall","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"spelling-not-meaning"},{"text":"mallet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"spelling-not-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$malnourished$q$, $q$Malnourished means "badly nourished," so mal- carries the meaning "bad" just as in malfunction, where a robot works badly and stops on its path. Mallet, mall, and malt only begin with the same letters and do not contain the prefix.$q$, 'draft', '6ba9277d-d8c4-5cce-84b0-02f02a456dc1')
