   $q$The prefix in- means "not," aud means "hear," and -ible means "able to be." What does it mean that the music was "inaudible" to the silent group?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It sounded unpleasant to the plants across the room","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It could not be heard by the plants across the room","is_correct":true},{"text":"It could not be seen by the plants across the room","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-root-meaning"},{"text":"It was too loud for the plants across the room","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It could not be heard by the plants across the room$q$, $q$In plus aud plus ible means "not able to be heard," which keeps the silent group truly silent for a fair test. "Too loud" ignores the prefix in-, which reverses the meaning of audible.$q$, 'draft', '7aa7f9ed-f054-5119-8f43-bc577d2cf370')
