   $q$The root bene means "good," and the suffix -ial means "having to do with." Why does Mr. Osei think the accident might be "beneficial"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It was part of the plan, because the partners wanted to move the plants all along.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It could lead to something good, because the partners can now study how light affects plants.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It could cause great harm, because the plants were pale and droopy on Monday.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It made the project shorter, because the partners no longer had to measure anything.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It could lead to something good, because the partners can now study how light affects plants.$q$, $q$Beneficial means "helpful" or "having a good effect," and Mr. Osei says scientists often learn the most from surprises, like the new finding about light. The plants were harmed, but the word describes the good result for the project, not the damage.$q$, 'draft', '7aa7f9ed-f054-5119-8f43-bc577d2cf370')
